{%- comment -%}
  PG RetroBox Tiles (2026-09-26): the PocketEra RetroBox page's offer tiles,
  cloned from sections/pg-pro2-tiles.liquid (the R36S Pro page) the same way
  pg-r36h-tiles was: the pack tiles' markup and styling, class prefix pg-p2 ->
  pg-rb, data-p2-* -> data-rb-*, script pgx-pg-retrobox-tiles.js.

  Registered in templates/product.pg-retrobox.json only.

  WHAT IS DIFFERENT FROM THE PRO 2. The RetroBox has ONE option, "Edition"
  (8-Bit Edition / 16-Bit Edition, same price), and no storage sizes, colours,
  bundles, duo discounts, protection kit or add-on cases. So:
    - there is one tile per EDITION, and the tile IS the variant picker: the
      selected tile is the variant Add to cart posts. No colour dropdowns
      (pgDrop), no 1 Console / Duo Pack switch, no add-on rows, no kit line;
    - the tiles are matched to the variants by the Edition value printed in
      data-rb-ed, so a variant that is missing or renamed simply leaves its
      tile out rather than selling the wrong thing;
    - the heading over the tiles reads "Choose Your Edition", not "Bundle &
      Save" (there is no bundle);
    - each tier note ends "plus an extra 5% off at checkout", as on the Pro 2
      (owner 2026-09-26: "make sure the 5% discount applies"). The store's
      automatic "Extra 5% off entire order" covers all items; a draft-order
      calculation of one of each edition took it ($239.98, -$11.99);
    - the pill on the big photo names the EDITION whose photo is showing (the
      Pro 2 names the colour), read from the product images' alt text, which
      starts "8-Bit Edition - ..." / "16-Bit Edition - ...". Any other photo
      (the hero of both consoles) carries the product's name instead, "Pocket
      Era RetroBox" (owner 2026-09-26);
    - picking an edition (its tile, or a button in the story) brings that
      edition's first photo up, on the big photo or in the phone carousel.

  WHAT IS STOOD DOWN ON THIS PAGE, AND WHY (unchanged from the Pro 2):
    - pgLadder (pg-theme-css) would build a Buy 2 Get 1 ladder, mirroring
      discounts this product does not carry. window.pgLadder is claimed first.
    - pgDuo (pg-theme-css) would decorate the first native tile. Claimed too.
    - pg-landing's own Single tile ([data-pgx-tile="single"]) is hidden by CSS
      and its #pgx-atc handler never runs: the window-capture listener in the
      script takes every Add to cart click first.
    - pg-tile-copy's generic .pgx-deal-note is hidden by the data-pg-tiernotes
      flag; each tile carries its own note instead.

  Prices are printed from the variants (Liquid, then repainted by the script),
  so they follow the admin: both editions are $119.99 against a $159.99
  compare-at (set 2026-09-26, owner: "make strikethrough price 159.99"), so
  each tile strikes $159.99 and its pill reads SAVE 25%. With no compare-at
  the strike and the SAVE pill go away by themselves.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign p = product -%}
{%- if p and p.variants.size > 0 -%}
{%- assign rb_v8 = nil -%}{%- assign rb_v16 = nil -%}
{%- for v in p.variants -%}
  {%- if v.option1 == '8-Bit Edition' -%}{%- assign rb_v8 = v -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if v.option1 == '16-Bit Edition' -%}{%- assign rb_v16 = v -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
<style>
  /* pg-landing's native single tile: replaced by the tiles below */
  #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-tile[data-pgx-tile="single"]{display:none !important}
  #pgx .pgx-tile.pg-rb{cursor:pointer}
  #pgx .pgx-tile.pg-rb .pgx-duo-t b{font-size:17px}
  /* the edition's name on the big photo: a pill centred over the top of the
     photo naming the edition whose shot is showing; the product's name on the
     shot of both consoles together */
  #pgx .pgx-hero{position:relative}
  /* on a phone pg-r36s-mobile hides the hero and turns the thumb strip into
     the swipe carousel (html.pg-r36-gal), so every edition SLIDE carries its
     own pill; the hero's pill serves the desktop */
  html.pg-r36-gal #pgx .pgx-thumbs > button{position:relative}
  #pgx .pgx-thumbs > button .pg-rb-hcap{display:none}
  html.pg-r36-gal #pgx .pgx-thumbs > button .pg-rb-hcap.on{display:inline-block}
  #pgx .pg-rb-hcap{position:absolute;left:50%;top:8px;transform:translateX(-50%);z-index:3;display:none;padding:9px 17px;border-radius:999px;white-space:nowrap;
    background:rgba(13,7,20,.74);border:1px solid rgba(199,155,234,.55);color:#fff;
    font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.05em;line-height:1;
    -webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(6px);backdrop-filter:blur(6px);pointer-events:none}
  #pgx .pg-rb-hcap.on{display:inline-block}
  /* the second tile sits close under the first, the hanging pill clears the box above */
  #pgx#pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-tile.pg-rb + .pgx-tile.pg-rb{margin-top:6px !important}
  #pgx .pg-rb .pg-rb-meta{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:6px;margin:7px 0 0}
  /* the chip sits at the tile's left edge beside the struck price when there is one */
  #pgx .pg-rb .pg-rb-meta{margin-top:-20px;padding-right:64px}
  #pgx .pg-rb .pg-rb-meta small{flex-basis:calc(100% + 64px)}
  /* no struck price (no compare-at set): the chip drops under the name instead of hugging the strike line */
  #pgx .pg-rb .pgx-duo-head:not(:has(s[data-rb-was]:not(:empty))) + .pg-rb-meta{margin-top:7px;padding-right:0}
  #pgx .pg-rb .pgx-duo-head:not(:has(s[data-rb-was]:not(:empty))) + .pg-rb-meta small{flex-basis:100%}
  #pgx .pg-rb .pg-rb-meta .pgx-lad-chip{display:inline-block !important;margin:0 !important}
  /* chip sizes as on the R36S Pro and Flip SP: 12.5px, 12px under 450px, 11.5px under 390px */
  #pgx#pgx .pg-rb .pg-rb-meta .pgx-lad-chip{font-size:12.5px !important}
  @media (max-width:449px){ #pgx#pgx .pg-rb .pg-rb-meta .pgx-lad-chip{font-size:12px !important;letter-spacing:0 !important;padding-left:8px !important;padding-right:8px !important} }
  @media (max-width:389px){
    #pgx#pgx .pg-rb .pg-rb-meta .pgx-lad-chip{font-size:11.5px !important}
    #pgx .pg-rb .pg-rb-meta{margin-top:5px;padding-right:0}
    #pgx .pg-rb .pg-rb-meta small{flex-basis:100%}
  }
  #pgx .pg-rb .pg-rb-meta small{flex:0 0 100%;display:block;margin:2px 0 0;font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.6;font-weight:600;color:#fff}
  /* what the edition includes: a two-column check list, shown on the selected
     tile like the tier note */
  #pgx .pg-rb-inc{display:none;width:max-content;max-width:100%;margin:12px auto 0;padding:0;list-style:none;grid-template-columns:auto auto;justify-content:center;gap:7px 24px}
  #pgx .pgx-tile.pgx-sel .pg-rb-inc{display:grid}
  #pgx .pg-rb-inc li{position:relative;padding-left:20px;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:600;color:#F1EDF7;line-height:1.3}
  #pgx .pg-rb-inc li:before{content:"\2713";position:absolute;left:0;top:0;color:#C79BEA;font-weight:800}
  #pgx .pg-rb-inc li b{font-weight:800}
  @media (max-width:389px){ #pgx .pg-rb .pg-rb-inc li{font-size:12px} }
  /* the line under the name stays on one line down to 375px */
  @media (max-width:380px){
    #pgx .pg-rb .pgx-duo-t small{font-size:12.5px}
  }
  @media (max-width:600px){
    #pgx .pg-rb-inc{gap:6px 14px}
    #pgx .pg-rb-inc li{font-size:12.5px;padding-left:17px;white-space:nowrap}
  }
</style>

<div class="pg-rb-src" id="pg-rb-src" hidden>
  {%- if rb_v8 -%}
  <div class="pgx-tile pgx-duo pg-rb pgx-sel" data-rb="e8" data-rb-ed="8-Bit Edition" data-rb-label="" role="radio" aria-checked="true" tabindex="0">
    <span class="pgx-lad-badge" data-rb-badge style="display:none"></span>
    <span class="pgx-duo-ribbon"></span>
    <div class="pgx-duo-head"><span class="pgx-duo-dot"></span>
      <div class="pgx-duo-t"><b>8-Bit Edition</b></div>
      <div class="pgx-duo-px"><b data-rb-now>{{ rb_v8.price | money }}</b><s data-rb-was>{%- if rb_v8.compare_at_price > rb_v8.price -%}{{ rb_v8.compare_at_price | money }}{%- endif -%}</s><span class="pgx-lad-chip pgx-each"></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-rb-meta"><span class="pgx-lad-chip">30 8-Bit Games &middot; 1 Controller</span><small>The grey classic, plugs into your TV</small></div>
    <ul class="pg-rb-inc">
      <li><b>30</b> Built-In Games</li>
      <li><b>1</b> Wired Controller</li>
      <li>HD Output via HDMI</li>
      <li>Save Your Progress</li>
      <li>18-Language Menu</li>
      <li>Free Shipping</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="pgx-tier-note"><b>One RetroBox 8-Bit Edition</b> with 30 classic 8-bit games built in and a wired controller, plus an extra <b>5% off</b> at checkout.</div>
  </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if rb_v16 -%}
  <div class="pgx-tile pgx-duo pg-rb{% unless rb_v8 %} pgx-sel{% endunless %}" data-rb="e16" data-rb-ed="16-Bit Edition" data-rb-label="2 PLAYERS" role="radio" aria-checked="{% if rb_v8 %}false{% else %}true{% endif %}" tabindex="0">
    <span class="pgx-lad-badge" data-rb-badge>2 PLAYERS</span>
    <span class="pgx-duo-ribbon"></span>
    <div class="pgx-duo-head"><span class="pgx-duo-dot"></span>
      <div class="pgx-duo-t"><b>16-Bit Edition</b></div>
      <div class="pgx-duo-px"><b data-rb-now>{{ rb_v16.price | money }}</b><s data-rb-was>{%- if rb_v16.compare_at_price > rb_v16.price -%}{{ rb_v16.compare_at_price | money }}{%- endif -%}</s><span class="pgx-lad-chip pgx-each"></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-rb-meta"><span class="pgx-lad-chip">30 16-Bit Games &middot; 2 Controllers</span><small>Purple buttons, built for 2 players</small></div>
    <ul class="pg-rb-inc">
      <li><b>30</b> Built-In Games</li>
      <li><b>2</b> Wired Controllers</li>
      <li>2-Player Ready</li>
      <li>HD Output via HDMI</li>
      <li>Save Your Progress</li>
      <li>Free Shipping</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="pgx-tier-note"><b>One RetroBox 16-Bit Edition</b> with 30 classic 16-bit games and two wired controllers for couch co-op, plus an extra <b>5% off</b> at checkout.</div>
  </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{%- comment -%} the pill on each product photo. An edition photo is one whose alt text STARTS with an Edition value: the part before " - " must equal a variant's Edition ("8-Bit Edition - ...", "16-Bit Edition - ..."). `contains` read the hero's "... 8-Bit and 16-Bit Editions" as the 16-Bit, so the photo of both consoles said "16-Bit Edition". Every photo is listed; the ones that are no edition's carry rb_name. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign rb_name = 'Pocket Era RetroBox' -%}
<script type="application/json" id="pg-rb-data">
{"variants":[{%- for v in p.variants -%}{"id":{{ v.id }},"e":{{ v.option1 | json }},"p":{{ v.price }},"cap":{{ v.compare_at_price | default: 0 }},"av":{{ v.available | json }}}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}{%- endfor -%}],"name":{{ rb_name | json }},"shots":[{%- for image in p.images -%}{%- assign rb_pre = image.alt | default: '' | split: ' – ' | first | split: ' - ' | first | strip | downcase -%}{%- assign rb_ed = '' -%}{%- for v in p.variants -%}{%- assign rb_vo = v.option1 | downcase -%}{%- if rb_pre != '' and rb_pre == rb_vo -%}{%- assign rb_ed = v.option1 -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}{"src":{{ image | image_url: width: 1400 | json }},"e":{{ rb_ed | json }}}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}{%- endfor -%}]}
</script>

<script src="{{ 'pgx-pg-retrobox-tiles.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
{%- endif -%}
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG RetroBox Tiles", "settings": [], "presets": [{"name": "PG RetroBox Tiles"}]}
{% endschema %}
